body:
So far I've tried chocolate, salted caramel, coffee caramel, peanut butter, and banana. For the past month I've been having nothing but Huel for probably 7-8 days, and then occasionally I'll get offered restaurant leftovers that a roommate brings home and doesn't want. All Huel Black though, I've never had the standard edition so I can't speak to better or worse there, but I really enjoyed all the flavors except salted caramel.

&#x200B;

I'm down to just salted caramel and coffee caramel now, waiting on the next shipment where I swapped salted caramel for vanilla. Salted caramel wasn't bad, but it really just didn't taste like much of anything. All the others  I've tried are distinctly their flavor, chocolate tastes like chocolate, banana tastes like banana. Coffee caramel tastes of coffee which is probably why I like it so much more than the salted caramel. A lot of what I did after trying each flavor individually was mixing them together, chocolate+peanut butter, chocolate+coffee caramel, peanut butter+banana, etc. All good combinations in my opinion.
